SwirlyMP - the SwirlOS video player (r47)
=========================================

Start it from the start menu, or double-click a video in Files.
It lists the videos it finds in ~/Videos, ~/, ~/desktop and /usb1.

Formats
  MPEG-1 video in an MPEG program stream (.mpg, .mpeg)
  Motion-JPEG video in an AVI container (.avi)
Audio tracks are recognised and skipped (the kernel has no mixer yet); the
player shows a "video only" notice. MPEG-2, H.264, MP4, MKV, MPEG-TS and
pictures above 1280x720 are refused with a readable reason.

Keys
  Space or K       play / pause           Left / Right   -5 s / +5 s
  J / L            -10 s / +10 s          Down / Up      -30 s / +30 s
  0                back to the start      R              loop on/off
  F                theater mode (Esc leaves it)
  O                open another video     Click the bar  seek
  Click the picture to play / pause. MPEG seeks land on the nearest keyframe.

Notes
  - One SwirlyMP window at a time (process slot 18, 16 MB).
  - Playback follows the wall clock: if the CPU is too slow Motion-JPEG drops
    frames, MPEG-1 slows down.
  - Files are streamed from disk, never loaded whole.

Third-party: MPEG-1 decoding uses pl_mpeg (MIT, Dominic Szablewski),
user/vendor/pl_mpeg.h, licence text in user/vendor/pl_mpeg.LICENSE.
JPEG frames use the system's IJG libjpeg.
